	abstract = {Berenger’s perfectly matched layer (PML) absorbing boundary condition for electromagnetic (EM) waves is derived t o a b s o r b 2-D a n d 3-D acoustic waves in finite difference t i m e d o m a i n ( F D T D ) simulation of acoustic wave propagation and scattering. A PML medium suitable for acoustic waves is constructed. Plane wave propagation in t h e P M L medium is solved for both 2-D and 3-D cases and explicit FDTD boundary conditions are derived. The equations show t h a t a matched P M L medium is a perfect simulation of free space in t h a t a plane wave does not change its direction of propagation or its speed w h e n it propagates from free space into a matched PML medium. F D T D simulation of a pulsed point source propagating in two dimensions is carried out t o test t h e performance of t h e P M L boundary for acoustic waves. Results show that an eight layer PML boundary condition reduces the reflected error 40 d B over Mur’s second order boundary condition.},
